From c7e8e2badc2cc307a40d26e73da4a541e9f1c418 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rae-ARK <horizonarkstudio@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 03:43:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add ARKtube session wiring for Cage, carried over from webtop

webtop's system overlay (session/overlay/overlay.py) was already
rewritten to depend on wlr-layer-shell-v1 support in 'the cage fork' --
this branch -- but nothing on this side actually assembled that into a
session you could log into and test. This closes that gap without
touching webtop:

- session/overlay/: the TV-style system overlay, vendored unchanged
  from webtop (it has no GNOME-Kiosk-specific code -- pure
  NetworkManager/PipeWire/upower/brightnessctl/loginctl calls).
- session/cage/arktube-cage-session: the session entry point, adapted
  from webtop's session/gnome-kiosk-script for Cage -- forks the
  overlay, then execs 'cage -d -- arktube_linux'. No
  KillMode=control-group systemd override needed the way GNOME Kiosk's
  session required: there's no gnome-session-binary layer here for
  Cage to sit inside of, and Cage's own sigchld_handler() already ends
  the session when arktube_linux exits.
- session/wayland-sessions/arktube-cage.desktop: a GDM gear-menu entry
  pointing straight at that script, not through gnome-session.
- session/install-arktube-cage-session.sh: builds this branch's Cage
  and deploys all of the above, including
  gir1.2-gtklayershell-0.1/libgtk-layer-shell0 -- a runtime dependency
  overlay.py has always had (gi.repository.GtkLayerShell) that webtop's
  own install-webtop-session.sh never actually installed, since it was
  dead weight under GNOME Kiosk/Mutter (xdg_toplevel gives no
  placement control there either) until this session made it load-
  bearing. Installs alongside, not instead of, webtop's existing GNOME
  Kiosk session, per CAGE-MIGRATION.md's own staged-cutover caution.
